"use strict";(self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith=self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith||[]).push([[31894],{831894:e=>{e.exports="---\nname: migration\ndescription: Power BI → Databricks AI/BI migration reference. Use when converting Power BI semantic models (DataModelSchema JSON or .pbit archives) into UC metric views, source SQL views, and AI/BI dashboards — covers DAX translation patterns, M-query → source SQL view classification, measure-container architecture, and per-page AI/BI dashboard build prompts.\n---\n\n# Power BI → AI/BI Migration\n\nMigration-specific logic plus a routing index to the detailed sub-skills. The system prompt owns the end-to-end workflow (Phases A–F) and the architectural decisions; this skill owns the translation rules, the M-query classification, the per-page sub-agent prompt template, and the architecture-pattern recipes.\n\n## The two-layer artifact stack\n\nEvery Power BI semantic model has two layers — a **storage layer** (the upstream UC tables the M-queries point at) and a **semantic-model layer** (what each Power BI table actually is after Power Query M-transformations and DAX calculated columns). DAX measures, calculated columns, and relationships all execute against the semantic-model layer, never against the raw storage layer.\n\nUC migrations reproduce both layers explicitly. From bottom to top:\n\n```\nmetric view (DAX measures + dimensions + joins)\n       │ source: / joins[].source:\n       ▼\nv_<table> source SQL view  ← when M-query has any non-trivial transform OR table has ≥1 materializable (\xa713.1) calc column\n       │ FROM\n       ▼\nupstream UC table          ← direct only when PASSTHROUGH AND zero materializable (\xa713.1) calc columns\n```\n\nA metric view's `source:` is the raw upstream **only** when the underlying Power BI table is PASSTHROUGH **and** has zero retained materializable (\xa713.1) calc columns. Pure `RELATED(...)` lifts (\xa713.2 — become metric-view joins) and untranslatable shapes (\xa713.3 — cascade aggregating measures to `lod_fixed` while the column itself is dropped) both leave the host PASSTHROUGH. In every other case `source:` is `<target_catalog>.<target_schema>.v_<table>` — the source view authored in Phase B.2. The same rule applies to every `joins[].source:`, classified per dimension table independently. Phase E executes bottom-up: source views first, then metric views, then dashboard pages.\n\nCalc-column DAX is **row-context** DAX, structurally different from the **filter-context** DAX that measures use. Only the row-context-safe subset enumerated in `dax-patterns.md` \xa713.1 (same-row scalar arithmetic, `IF` / `SWITCH` / `DIVIDE` over row fields, scalar text/date funcs, null coalescing) translates to a SQL derived column. Pure `RELATED(...)` lifts (\xa713.2) become metric-view joins. Every other shape (\xa713.3 — aggregation funcs, `CALCULATE`, `FILTER`, measure references, `EARLIER`, table-valued ops) is untranslatable and cascades each aggregating measure to `cannot_migrate` / `lod_fixed`.\n\n`source-views.md` \xa71 owns the M-query → bucket decision; `pbi-schema.md` \xa7\"Calculated columns\" owns the calc-column rules and the reclassification trigger; `architecture-patterns.md` \xa79 owns the source-reference policy that ties them together; `dax-patterns.md` (preamble + \xa713) owns the row-context translation subset.\n\n## Coverage at a Glance\n\n| Category             | Coverage                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            | Detail                                 |\n| -------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------- |\n| Tables               | fact / dimension / measure container ✅; config-lookup ⚠️ (materialize when dashboards need it); internal-PBI ❌                                                                                                                                                                                                                    | `pbi-schema.md`                        |\n| M-query upstream     | `Databricks.Catalogs` passthrough ✅; `Value.NativeQuery` and Power-Query transforms → source views ✅; `Table.FromRows` empty-container ✅ (fan measures out, don't reify); `Table.FromRows` real lookup ⚠️; `Dataflows` / `entity` ❌ (3-way upstream prompt)                                                                     | `source-views.md`                      |\n| DAX measures         | leaf aggregations ✅; `DIVIDE` → `CASE WHEN` ✅; `CALCULATE` with `FILTER (WHERE ...)` ✅; measure references → `MEASURE()` ✅; `RELATED` → joins ✅; time intelligence ⚠️ (window-measure workarounds where covered)                                                                                                               | `dax-patterns.md`                      |\n| Calculated columns   | row-context-safe scalars (\xa713.1: arithmetic, `IF`/`SWITCH`/`DIVIDE`, scalar text/date) → derived columns in `v_<table>` ✅; pure `RELATED` lifts (\xa713.2) → metric-view joins ✅; aggregation funcs / `CALCULATE` / `FILTER` / measure refs / `EARLIER` / table-valued ops (\xa713.3) ❌ (cascades aggregating measures to `lod_fixed`) | `pbi-schema.md`, `dax-patterns.md` \xa713 |\n| DAX patterns to skip | `ALLSELECTED`, `USERELATIONSHIP`, `EXTERNALMEASURE`, `USERPRINCIPALNAME`, `ISFILTERED`, `CONCATENATEX`, `SELECTEDVALUE` as guard ❌                                                                                                                                                                                                 | `dax-unsupported.md`                   |\n| Architecture         | one MV per fact-domain (not per fact-table); measure containers fan out by inferred DAX home; periodic source-pair unification; config scalars → dashboard layer                                                                                                                                                                    | `architecture-patterns.md`             |\n| Visualizations       | per-page sub-agent dispatch via `sub_dashboardagent`; Power BI visual → AI/BI widget mapping; slicer → AI/BI filter widget                                                                                                                                                                                                          | `dashboard-build.md`                   |\n| Parameters / What-If | Skipped — no metric-view equivalent                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 | —                                      |\n| RLS roles            | Skipped — out of scope; consider UC row access policies as a follow-up                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              | —                                      |\n| `.pbix` binaries     | Skipped — only `.pbit` and standalone DataModelSchema JSON                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          | —                                      |\n\n## Skip Criteria\n\nApply this decision tree to every measure:\n\n```\nIF expression contains a parameter reference ([Parameters.X])\n  → SKIP: parameter — no metric-view equivalent\n\nELSE IF expression uses any unsupported DAX function\n       (ALLSELECTED, USERELATIONSHIP, EXTERNALMEASURE, USERPRINCIPALNAME,\n        ISFILTERED, CONCATENATEX, SELECTEDVALUE-as-guard)\n  → Classify per dax-unsupported.md:\n    - ALLSELECTED                              → SKIP or migrate as window measure (range: all)\n    - USERELATIONSHIP                          → MIGRATE via separate join paths or per-relationship MVs\n    - Rolling / YTD time intelligence          → MIGRATE via window measures (TOTALYTD → cumulative range;\n       (TOTALYTD, DATESINPERIOD, etc.)            DATESINPERIOD → trailing range)\n    - Point-shifted time intelligence          → SKIP or migrate via source-view precomputation\n       (SAMEPERIODLASTYEAR, PARALLELPERIOD)       (a `trailing` window is NOT equivalent — it aggregates the\n                                                  prior range, not the same shifted period)\n    - ISFILTERED / CONCATENATEX /              → SKIP (display-layer)\n       SELECTEDVALUE-as-guard\n\nELSE IF expression is SWITCH(SELECTEDVALUE(...), ...) slicer-dispatch\n  → DECOMPOSE into separate measures (one per branch); have the dashboard\n    slicer drive widget selection or a filter dimension. See\n    architecture-patterns.md \xa72.\n\nELSE\n  → translate per dax-patterns.md\n  → if no rule matches, SKIP: no_skill_rule (surface prominently in the\n    final report so the skill set can be extended).\n```\n\nWhen uncertain about any measure, SKIP — it's the safe default. The system prompt's failure protocol records each skipped measure with its reason.\n\n## Skip Documentation Format\n\nDocument every skipped item in the metric view's top-level `comment:` field (NOT as `#` line comments — UC ignores those). One skipped item per line:\n\n```yaml\ncomment: |\n  Migrated from Power BI semantic model \"Sales Dashboard\".\n  Skipped measures:\n  - SKIPPED: Sales 2024 Only; Reason: complex_filter_context — CALCULATE with FILTER+ALL has no metric-view equivalent; Original: CALCULATE([Sales], FILTER(ALL('Date'), 'Date'[Year] = 2024))\n  - SKIPPED: User Email; Reason: parameter — USERPRINCIPALNAME() has no metric-view equivalent; consider UC row access policies\n  - SKIPPED: Sales Same Period LY; Reason: time_intelligence — SAMEPERIODLASTYEAR has no metric-view equivalent; precompute prior-year amount in a source view via LAG / self-join, or skip\n```\n\nSlicer-dispatch measures (`SWITCH(SELECTEDVALUE(...), ...)`) are not skipped — they're decomposed into per-branch measures in the metric view (see `architecture-patterns.md` \xa72) and the slicer is reproduced as an AI/BI filter widget. Document those in a separate `Decomposed measures:` block in the same `comment:` field rather than under `Skipped measures:`.\n\n## Power BI ↔ AI/BI Conceptual Map\n\n| Concept             | Power BI                                               | UC Metric View / AI/BI                                                           |\n| ------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Field reference     | `Table[Column]` or `'Table'[Column]`                   | `source.column` (or aliased table reference inside an MV with joins)             |\n| Measure reference   | `[MeasureName]`                                        | `MEASURE(measure_name)`                                                          |\n| Aggregation         | Implicit via measure DAX                               | Explicit YAML `expr:` with `SUM`, `COUNT`, `AVG`, `MIN`, `MAX`, `COUNT DISTINCT` |\n| Safe division       | `DIVIDE(num, den, 0)`                                  | `CASE WHEN MEASURE(den) = 0 THEN 0 ELSE MEASURE(num) / MEASURE(den) END`         |\n| Conditional         | `IF(cond, a, b)`                                       | `CASE WHEN cond THEN a ELSE b END`                                               |\n| Null coalesce       | `IF(ISBLANK(x), 0, x)`                                 | `COALESCE(MEASURE(x), 0)`                                                        |\n| Distinct count      | `DISTINCTCOUNT(table[col])` / `COUNTROWS(VALUES(...))` | `COUNT(DISTINCT source.col)`                                                     |\n| Filter on aggregate | `CALCULATE(SUM(...), FILTER(t, ...))`                  | `SUM(source.x) FILTER (WHERE source.y = '...')`                                  |\n| Cross-table column  | `RELATED(dim[attr])`                                   | `joins:` with the dim table; reference `dim.attr` directly                       |\n| Format string       | `formatString: \"$#,##0.00\"`                            | YAML `format:` block (`type: currency`, `currency_code: USD`, `decimal_places`)  |\n\nPer-pattern translation lives in `dax-patterns.md`; the unsupported list is in `dax-unsupported.md`.\n\n## Files\n\n| File                                                 | Use when                                                                                                                                                                                |\n| ---------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| [pbi-schema.md](pbi-schema.md)                       | Walking the parsed DataModelSchema JSON: tables, columns, measures, relationships, partition source kinds.                                                                              |\n| [source-views.md](source-views.md)                   | Classifying each table's M-query upstream (4 buckets); generating source SQL views; the 3-way upstream-resolution prompt; periodic-source-pair unification.                             |\n| [architecture-patterns.md](architecture-patterns.md) | Architectural decisions before translation: unify vs split; slicer-dispatch routing; config-scalars → dashboard; cross-fact handling; dimension completeness; cross-catalog references. |\n| [dax-patterns.md](dax-patterns.md)                   | Translating individual DAX expressions to metric-view YAML measure expressions.                                                                                                         |\n| [dax-unsupported.md](dax-unsupported.md)             | Recognizing patterns that cannot migrate, with workarounds where they exist.                                                                                                            |\n| [dashboard-build.md](dashboard-build.md)             | Phase E — writing per-page prompts for the `sub_dashboardagent` AI/BI dashboard authoring sub-agent.                                                                                    |\n\nLoad only the file matching your current step. The system prompt directs you here when needed.\n"}}]);
